    Bug 1772455 - Prevent deeply nested thread messages from disappearing. r=tobyp


    The `m_levels` arrays across the nsMsgDBView implementations were previously
    defined as `nsTArray<uint8_t>`. When a thread reached a nesting depth greater
    than 255, the `uint32_t` depth parameter was implicitly truncated during
    insertion. This overflow caused the view builder to misinterpret the tree
    hierarchy and drop the subsequent messages from the UI entirely.

    This patch resolves the issue by upgrading `m_levels`, `m_prevLevels`, and
    their associated local iterator variables from `uint8_t` to `uint32_t` to
    match the public API signatures.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D300525

